cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LunaLink: an open reference implementation of the LunaNet Augmented Forward Signal"
message: "If you use LunaLink in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marco
    family-names: Fiscato
    email: marco.fiscato@gmail.com
    affiliation: Luar Space
repository-code: "https://github.com/luar-space/lunalink"
url: "https://luar-space.github.io/lunalink/"
abstract: >-
  LunaLink is an open-source reference implementation of the LunaNet
  Signal-In-Space Recommended Standard for the Augmented Forward Signal
  (LSIS V1.0). It implements the complete transmit chain (Gold-2046 and
  Weil-10230 spreading codes, CRC-24Q, BCH(51,8), LDPC, block interleaving,
  BPSK modulation and I/Q multiplexing) and the inverse receive chain
  (frame synchronisation by cross-correlation, soft-decision decoding, and
  navigation message parsing), together with Signal-In-Space Error
  computation. The C++20 core is written to a flight-software dialect
  unioning MISRA C++:2023, the JPL Institutional Coding Standard and
  NASA and ESA coding practice, and carries a mission assurance case
  including a software FMEA and fault-injection evidence. Python bindings
  are provided via nanobind.
keywords:
  - LunaNet
  - Augmented Forward Signal
  - lunar navigation
  - satellite navigation
  - GNSS
  - CCSDS
  - software-defined radio
  - LDPC
  - flight software
  - reference implementation
license: Apache-2.0
